{"id":"mahabharata-9-014","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":14,"title":"चतुर्दशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 14 · Duryodhana and Dhrishtadyumna fight","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana and Dhrishtadyumna fight a great duel, and Satyaki takes another chariot to aid the Pandavas. Shalya's chariot moves about the battlefield as before.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ-ಧೃಷ್ಟದ್ಯುಮ್ನರು ಮಹಾ ದ್ವಂದ್ವ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಸಾತ್ಯಕಿ ಬೇರೆ ರಥ ಏರಿ ಪಾಂಡವರಿಗೆ ಸಹಾಯ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಲ್ಯನ ರಥ ಮೊದಲಿನಂತೆ ರಣರಂಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಸಂಚರಿಸುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन और धृष्टद्युम्न महान द्वन्द्व करते हैं, और सात्यकि दूसरा रथ लेकर पाण्डवों की सहायता करता है। शल्य का रथ पहले की तरह रणभूमि में विचरता है।","te":"దుర్యోధనుడు, ధృష్టద్యుమ్నుడు మహా ద్వంద్వం చేస్తారు; సాత్యకి మరో రథం ఎక్కి పాండవులకు సాయం చేస్తాడు. శల్యుని రథం మునుపటిలా రణభూమిలో తిరుగుతుంది.","ta":"துரியோதனனும் த்ருஷ்டத்யும்னனும் பெரும் தனிப்போர் புரிகின்றனர்; சாத்யகி வேறு தேரில் ஏறிப் பாண்டவருக்கு உதவுகிறான். சல்யனின் தேர் முன்போல் களத்தில் சுழல்கிறது.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനനും ധൃഷ്ടദ്യുമ്നനും തമ്മിൽ ഘോരയുദ്ധം നടക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവരെ സഹായിക്കാൻ സാത്യകി മറ്റൊരു രഥമെടുക്കുന്നു. ശല്യന്റെ രഥം മുൻപത്തെപ്പോലെ യുദ്ധക്കളത്തിൽ ചുറ്റിക്കറങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.14; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दुर्योधनो महाराज धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ।\nचक्रतुः सुमहद्युद्धं शरशक्तिसमाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana and Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata, fought a very great fight, thick with arrows and lances, great king."}},{"n":2,"text":"तयोरासन्महाराज शरधाराः सहस्रशः ।\nअम्बुदानां यथा काले जलधाराः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Between them, great king, there were thousands of streams of arrows, like streams of water from clouds in their season, all around."}},{"n":3,"text":"राजा तु पार्षतं विद्ध्वा शरैः पञ्चभिरायसैः ।\nद्रोणहन्तारमुग्रेषुः पुनर्विव्याध सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, with fierce arrows, pierced the son of Prishata, the slayer of Drona, with five iron arrows and then again with seven."}},{"n":4,"text":"धृष्टद्युम्नस्तु समरे बलवान्दृढविक्रमः ।\nसप्तत्या विशिखानां वै दुर्योधनमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtadyumna, strong and firm in prowess, tormented Duryodhana with seventy arrows in the battle."}},{"n":5,"text":"पीडितं प्रेक्ष्य राजानं सोदर्या भरतर्षभ ।\nमहत्या सेनया सार्धं परिवव्रुः स्म पार्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king hard pressed, his brothers, best of Bharatas, with a great army surrounded the son of Prishata."}},{"n":6,"text":"स तैः परिवृतः शूरैः सर्वतोऽतिरथैर्भृशम् ।\nव्यचरत्समरे राजन्दर्शयन्हस्तलाघवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounded on all sides by those brave and surpassing warriors, he moved about in the battle, O king, showing his quickness of hand."}},{"n":7,"text":"शिखण्डी कृतवर्माणं गौतमं च महारथम् ।\nप्रभद्रकैः समायुक्तो योधयामास धन्विनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shikhandi, joined by the Prabhadrakas, fought the two archers, Kritavarman and the great warrior Kripa the Gautama."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्रापि सुमहद्युद्धं घोररूपं विशां पते ।\nप्राणान्संत्यजतां युद्धे प्राणद्यूताभिदेवने ॥","meaning":{"en":"There too a great and fearsome fight took place, lord of men, of men who staked their lives in the gamble of battle."}},{"n":9,"text":"शल्यस्तु शरवर्षाणि विमुञ्चन्सर्वतोदिशम् ।\nपाण्डवान्पीडयामास ससात्यकिवृकोदरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, loosing showers of arrows in every direction, harried the Pandavas, with Satyaki and Bhima among them."}},{"n":10,"text":"तथोभौ च यमौ युद्धे यमतुल्यपराक्रमौ ।\nयोधयामास राजेन्द्र वीर्येण च बलेन च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He fought also the two twins, whose prowess in battle was like Yama's, with his might and strength, king of kings."}},{"n":11,"text":"शल्यसायकनुन्नानां पाण्डवानां महामृधे ।\nत्रातारं नाध्यगच्छन्त केचित्तत्र महारथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that great battle, the Pandavas, driven back by Shalya's arrows, found no protector among the great warriors there."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततस्तु नकुलः शूरो धर्मराजे प्रपीडिते ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन मातुलं माद्रिनन्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then brave Nakula, son of Madri, when Yudhishthira was hard pressed, rushed swiftly at his maternal uncle."}},{"n":13,"text":"संछाद्य समरे शल्यं नकुलः परवीरहा ।\nविव्याध चैनं दशभिः स्मयमानः स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Covering Shalya in the battle, Nakula, slayer of enemy heroes, smiling, pierced him with ten arrows in the chest."}},{"n":14,"text":"सर्वपारशवैर्बाणैः कर्मारपरिमार्जितैः ।\nस्वर्णपुङ्खैः शिलाधौतैर्धनुर्यन्त्रप्रचोदितैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were steel arrows polished by smiths, gold-feathered, washed on stone and driven from the bow's string."}},{"n":15,"text":"शल्यस्तु पीडितस्तेन स्वस्रीयेण महात्मना ।\nनकुलं पीडयामास पत्रिभिर्नतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, hurt by his great-souled sister's son, hurt Nakula in turn with feathered arrows with bent joints."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा भीमसेनोऽथ सात्यकिः ।\nसहदेवश्च माद्रेयो मद्रराजमुपाद्रवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, Bhimasena, Satyaki and Sahadeva, the son of Madri, rushed at the king of Madras."}},{"n":17,"text":"तानापतत एवाशु पूरयानान्रथस्वनैः ।\nदिशश्च प्रदिशश्चैव कम्पयानांश्च मेदिनीम् ।\nप्रतिजग्राह समरे सेनापतिरमित्रजित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they attacked, filling the directions with the rattle of chariots and shaking the earth, the commander, the vanquisher of foes, met them in the battle."}},{"n":18,"text":"युधिष्ठिरं त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा भीमसेनं च सप्तभिः ।\nसात्यकिं च शतेनाजौ सहदेवं त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Yudhishthira with three arrows, Bhimasena with seven, Satyaki with a hundred in the fight, and Sahadeva with three."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततस्तु सशरं चापं नकुलस्य महात्मनः ।\nमद्रेश्वरः क्षुरप्रेण तदा चिच्छेद मारिष ।\nतदशीर्यत विच्छिन्नं धनुः शल्यस्य सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord of Madra, my lord, cut the bow and arrow of the great-souled Nakula with a razor-edged arrow, and that bow, cut, was shattered by Shalya's arrows."}},{"n":20,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय माद्रीपुत्रो महारथः ।\nमद्रराजरथं तूर्णं पूरयामास पत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great warrior, son of Madri, took another bow and quickly filled the king of Madras's chariot with feathered arrows."}},{"n":21,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु मद्रेशं सहदेवश्च मारिष ।\nदशभिर्दशभिर्बाणैरुरस्येनमविध्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira and Sahadeva, my lord, pierced the lord of Madra in the chest with ten arrows each."}},{"n":22,"text":"भीमसेनस्ततः षष्ट्या सात्यकिर्नवभिः शरैः ।\nमद्रराजमभिद्रुत्य जघ्नतुः कङ्कपत्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhimasena with sixty and Satyaki with nine arrows rushed at the king of Madras and struck him with heron-feathered shafts."}},{"n":23,"text":"मद्रराजस्ततः क्रुद्धः सात्यकिं नवभिः शरैः ।\nविव्याध भूयः सप्तत्या शराणां नतपर्वणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the angry king of Madras pierced Satyaki with nine arrows, and again with seventy arrows with bent joints."}},{"n":24,"text":"अथास्य सशरं चापं मुष्टौ चिच्छेद मारिष ।\nहयांश्च चतुरः संख्ये प्रेषयामास मृत्यवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, my lord, he cut Satyaki's bow and arrow in his fist, and sent his four horses to death in the battle."}},{"n":25,"text":"विरथं सात्यकिं कृत्वा मद्रराजो महाबलः ।\nविशिखानां शतेनैनमाजघान समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made Satyaki chariotless, the strong king of Madras struck him all over with a hundred arrows."}},{"n":26,"text":"माद्रीपुत्रौ तु संरब्धौ भीमसेनं च पाण्डवम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं च कौरव्य विव्याध दशभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged, he pierced the two sons of Madri, Bhimasena the Pandava and Yudhishthira with ten arrows each, Kaurava."}},{"n":27,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम मद्रराजस्य पौरुषम् ।\nयदेनं सहिताः पार्था नाभ्यवर्तन्त संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a wonder of the Madra king's prowess, that the sons of Pritha, though together, could not stand against him in the fight."}},{"n":28,"text":"अथान्यं रथमास्थाय सात्यकिः सत्यविक्रमः ।\nपीडितान्पाण्डवान्दृष्ट्वा मद्रराजवशं गतान् ।\nअभिदुद्राव वेगेन मद्राणामधिपं बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Satyaki, true in valor, climbed onto another chariot, and seeing the Pandavas hard pressed and in the power of the king of Madras, the strong man rushed swiftly at the lord of the Madras."}},{"n":29,"text":"आपतन्तं रथं तस्य शल्यः समितिशोभनः ।\nप्रत्युद्ययौ रथेनैव मत्तो मत्तमिव द्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, the pride of assemblies, met his oncoming chariot with his own, like one rutting elephant meeting another."}},{"n":30,"text":"स संनिपातस्तुमुलो बभूवाद्भुतदर्शनः ।\nसात्यकेश्चैव शूरस्य मद्राणामधिपस्य च ।\nयादृशो वै पुरा वृत्तः शम्बरामरराजयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The clash was tumultuous and wonderful to see, between brave Satyaki and the lord of Madra, like the old one between Shambara and the king of the gods."}},{"n":31,"text":"सात्यकिः प्रेक्ष्य समरे मद्रराजं व्यवस्थितम् ।\nविव्याध दशभिर्बाणैस्तिष्ठ तिष्ठेति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king of Madras standing in the battle, Satyaki pierced him with ten arrows and said, \"Stand, stand!\""}},{"n":32,"text":"मद्रराजस्तु सुभृशं विद्धस्तेन महात्मना ।\nसात्यकिं प्रतिविव्याध चित्रपुङ्खैः शितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply pierced by that great-souled man, the king of Madras struck Satyaki back with sharp, bright-feathered arrows."}},{"n":33,"text":"ततः पार्था महेष्वासाः सात्वताभिसृतं नृपम् ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्रथैस्तूर्णं मातुलं वधकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Pandavas, great archers, quickly charged in their chariots at the king, who had gone against the Satvata, wanting to kill their maternal uncle."}},{"n":34,"text":"तत आसीत्परामर्दस्तुमुलः शोणितोदकः ।\nशूराणां युध्यमानानां सिंहानामिव नर्दताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was then a tumultuous grinding fight, with blood for water, of brave men fighting like roaring lions."}},{"n":35,"text":"तेषामासीन्महाराज व्यतिक्षेपः परस्परम् ।\nसिंहानामामिषेप्सूनां कूजतामिव संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They hurled weapons at one another, great king, like lions in the fight roaring for meat."}},{"n":36,"text":"तेषां बाणसहस्रौघैराकीर्णा वसुधाभवत् ।\nअन्तरिक्षं च सहसा बाणभूतमभूत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was strewn with their thousands of arrows, and the sky suddenly seemed made of arrows."}},{"n":37,"text":"शरान्धकारं बहुधा कृतं तत्र समन्ततः ।\nअभ्रच्छायेव संजज्ञे शरैर्मुक्तैर्महात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everywhere the darkness of arrows was made many times over, and it seemed a cloud-shadow from the arrows released by those great-souled men."}},{"n":38,"text":"तत्र राजञ्शरैर्मुक्तैर्निर्मुक्तैरिव पन्नगैः ।\nस्वर्णपुङ्खैः प्रकाशद्भिर्व्यरोचन्त दिशस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O king, the directions shone with the gold-feathered arrows, gleaming like snakes that have shed their skins."}},{"n":39,"text":"तत्राद्भुतं परं चक्रे शल्यः शत्रुनिबर्हणः ।\nयदेकः समरे शूरो योधयामास वै बहून् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Shalya, slayer of foes, did a very great wonder: that alone he fought many in the battle."}},{"n":40,"text":"मद्रराजभुजोत्सृष्टैः कङ्कबर्हिणवाजितैः ।\nसंपतद्भिः शरैर्घोरैरवाकीर्यत मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was strewn with fearsome falling arrows loosed from the king of Madras's arm, fletched with heron and peacock feathers."}},{"n":41,"text":"तत्र शल्यरथं राजन्विचरन्तं महाहवे ।\nअपश्याम यथा पूर्वं शक्रस्यासुरसंक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"There, O king, we saw Shalya's chariot moving about in that great battle as we had seen Indra's of old in the destruction of the asuras."}}]}]}